# The scenes of the dynamic-tests deck, in order. Each "## Scene N: title" is one slide, spoken with item N of
# dynamic-tests.narration.md. Each line under a heading puts one thing on the slide:
#   note "<text>"         a line of text
#   show <file> ...       a code panel: <from> <to> or /pattern/, then a label; --mark and --zoom mark lines
#   run_live "<command>"  a live run, played from its cast in dynamic-tests.outputs/
#   callout "<text>"      a boxed sentence saying what a result means

## Scene 1: the examples
note "A folder of *examples*: each file holds a customer record, and the name expected on a letter."
show lessons/dynamic-tests/example/src/test/resources/examples/apostrophe.txt 1 2 "one example file"

## Scene 2: the code under test
note "The code under test: today's name formatter. It capitalises the first letter of each word."
show TodaysNameFormatter 11 16 "today's formatter" --zoom 14

## Scene 3: one test for all
note "*One test* loops over every example."
show AllExamplesInOneTest 12 18 "one test for every example" --zoom 14-16

## Scene 4: a test for each
note "A *test factory* makes one test for each example file, named after the file."
show EachExampleTest 13 20 "one test for each example" --zoom 15-16
show Formatters 33 42 "every file in the folder" --mark 35-36

## Scene 5: every failure named
note "Run the tests against today's formatter:"
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:dynamic-tests:test -Pcode=today"
callout "The loop shows one failure, then stops. The factory names all three: apostrophes and hyphens."

## Scene 6: the fixed formatter
note "The formatter that starts a word after a space, hyphen or apostrophe:"
show LetterNameFormatter 14 22 "the fixed formatter" --zoom 19
run_live "./gradlew :lessons:dynamic-tests:test"
callout "Every example passes. A new example is just a new file: no new test code."
